## Re-scope (2026-05-27)

The first execution attempt is **abandoned**: it hit two report figures that
cannot be regenerated (`fig_census_direct`, `fig_base_vs_census`) because the
`prompt_version` tag was dropped in the 0297/0344 mart rebuild. Rather than
recover or freeze them, ticket **0358** deletes the whole Experiment-3 / ablation
thread (and the stale `fig_census_direct`). This ticket is **Blocked-by 0358** and
runs **after** it, on the already-pruned tree. The charter below is unchanged — no
`uv run` in `make report` — but the migration inventory shrinks: every ablation
artifact in "Relevant files" below is **removed by 0358, not migrated**
(`fig_census_direct`, `tab_base_vs_census`, `fig_ablation_strip`,
`fig_ablation_heatmap`, `plot_ablation`). What remains to migrate into
`experiments/analysis.mk`: `tab_census`, `macros`, `tab_relances`,
`tab_comparaison`, `tab_variance`, `tab_verification`, and the other regenerable
handoff artifacts.

## Context

Ticket 0345 collapsed the **slides** writing build to consume committed
handoff artifacts only (no `uv run`, no data access), honoring the
analysis/writing workpackage split in `.claude/rules/coding-python.md`.

A celebrate-phase sweep found the **report** side still has the same
anti-pattern: the root `Makefile`'s `report/report.pdf` target depends on
~10–13 prerequisites that each have `uv run` recipes. So `make report`
triggers Python data analysis (tabulate_census, plot_ablation,
tabulate_variance, etc.) — it is NOT clean-room. The `report/Makefile`
sub-build itself is clean (no `uv run`), but the root `report/report.pdf`
rule pulls analysis in directly.

This is post-conference work (the 2026-05-27 talk is slides-driven; the
report stays exploratory, paper writing opens after the talk). Not urgent,
but it closes the workpackage-split loophole symmetrically with 0345.

## Relevant files
- `Makefile` — `report/report.pdf` target (~line 216) and its `uv run`
  prerequisite rules (tab_census, macros, tab_relances, tab_comparaison,
  tab_variance, tab_verification, fig_census_direct, tab_base_vs_census,
  fig_ablation_strip, fig_ablation_heatmap, etc.)
- `experiments/analysis.mk` — the analysis workpackage; missing report-side
  producers should move here (mirror the 0345 pattern)
- `report/Makefile` — already clean; consumes committed artifacts
- `.claude/rules/coding-python.md` — Build section, workpackage-split rule

## Actions
1. Inventory every prerequisite of `report/report.pdf` in the root Makefile.
   Classify each as: (a) committed handoff artifact with no recipe, or
   (b) `uv run` analysis rule.
2. For each (b): move the generation rule into `experiments/analysis.mk`
   (or the appropriate analysis driver), generate the artifact, and commit
   it as a handoff artifact. Remove the `uv run` rule from the root Makefile.
3. Verify `report/report.pdf` then depends only on committed files.
4. Confirm `report/Makefile` still compiles the PDF from committed inputs
   with no recursive `$(MAKE) -C ..` that re-triggers analysis.

## Test
Clean-room check: from a fresh checkout with no Python env / no `.venv`,
`make -C report report.pdf` (or the report sub-build) compiles using only
committed artifacts — zero `uv run` invocations. Capture the make dry-run
(`make -n report`) and assert no line contains `uv run`.

## Verification
- [ ] `make -n report` shows no `uv run` in the recipe trace
- [ ] All `report/report.pdf` prerequisites are committed (verify each via
      `git cat-file -e HEAD:<path>`)
- [ ] Report-side analysis rules now live in `experiments/analysis.mk`
- [ ] `experiments/analysis.mk` regenerates the report artifacts end-to-end

## Invariants
- Do not break `make slides` (0345's clean-room property must hold)
- `make check` passes
- The committed report figures/tables remain byte-equivalent (or visually
  equivalent) after regeneration from the analysis build

## Exit criteria
- `make report` (writing build) contains no `uv run` / data-access rules —
  compiles from committed handoff artifacts only
- `experiments/analysis.mk` is the sole producer of report figures/tables
- `make check` passes
